<article class="env-lemma" id="0AT1">
  <p><a class="environment-identifier" href="/tag/0AT1">Lemma <span data-tag="0AT1">38.25.2</span>.</a> If in Situation <a href="/tag/0AT0" data-tag="0AT0">38.25.1</a> the ring $A$ is Noetherian then the lemma holds. </p>
</article><article class="env-proof">
    <p>
      <strong>Proof.</strong>
      Applying Algebra, Lemma <a href="/tag/00ME" data-tag="00ME">10.99.1</a> we see that $u$ is injective and that $N/u(M)$ is flat over $A$. Then $u$ is $A$-universally injective (Algebra, Lemma <a href="/tag/00HL" data-tag="00HL">10.39.12</a>) and $N$ is $A$-flat (Algebra, Lemma <a href="/tag/00HM" data-tag="00HM">10.39.13</a>). Since $B$ is Noetherian in this case we see that $N$ is of finite presentation. 
      <span class="qed">$\square$</span>
    </p>
